WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.830
Around 1168, in Old Cairo, a rabbi
finished a commentary on the Mishnah.

2
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:10.350
In it, Maimonides set out thirteen
foundations of Jewish faith.

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.750
The first five are about God.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.630
One says God is without a body.

5
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.140
Yet the Torah speaks of God's right hand,

6
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.190
God's eyes, and a voice from the fire.

7
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.770
So why does the Torah talk this way?

8
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.270
In this mission, you'll meet
all five principles about God,

9
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.530
and the Tanakh verses behind them.

10
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.920
Then you'll see what they mean for prayer:

11
00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:35.600
who receives it, and whether
anyone may carry it to God.

12
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:39.300
Your mission: find out why
the Torah gives God a hand,

13
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.830
eyes and a voice.
